@startuml
title LockHandle Lifecycle State
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

state "ACQUIRED\nlease + ownerToken" as ACQUIRED
state "ACTIVE\nnot lost\nnot releaseAttempted" as ACTIVE
state "LOST\nlock known lost" as LOST
state "RELEASE_ATTEMPTED\nlocal release attempted" as RELEASED
state "CLOSED" as CLOSED

[*] --> ACQUIRED
ACQUIRED --> ACTIVE : LockHandle created
ACTIVE --> ACTIVE : checkHeld=HELD / renew=RENEWED
ACTIVE --> LOST : check/renew/release returns NOT_FOUND or NOT_OWNER
ACTIVE --> RELEASED : unlock/releaseWithOutcome first call
LOST --> RELEASED : unlock after lost
RELEASED --> CLOSED : watchdog stopped
ACTIVE --> LOST : watchdog maxRenewTime exceeded

note right of ACTIVE
LockLease is immutable.
LockRuntimeState stores lost and releaseAttempted flags.
end note

note bottom of LOST
LOST and RELEASE_ATTEMPTED are not mutually exclusive concepts.
A handle may become lost and later release may still be attempted.
end note
@enduml
